2020-01-01 (8h!)
A record summary can span
multiple lines and carry tags like #outdoors
    +3m Duration with explicit plus sign
    8:30 - 10:30 Layout draft #project=478
    10:30 - 12:00 Phone #call="Liz Jones"
    5h A short summary.
    -120m This is a longer summary, which
        is continued on the next line.
    14:00 - ?
        Summaries can also start on the
        subsequent line.

2020/01/02 (-3h30m!)
    <23:00 - 2:00 Started the day before
    22:00 - 3:00> Ended the day after
    9:30am - 5:45pm Twelve-hour clock
    23:00 - 24:00 Until midnight
    1h30m #home-office #読む
    45m #project='single quotes' #unicode-tag_1

2020-01-03
	1h Tab indentation
	0h Zero duration
	10:00-??? Aligned open range

2020-01-06 (7h30m!)
Two spaces of indentation. With it, entry summaries
continue with four spaces.
  8:00 - 12:15 Sprint planning #project=478 #meeting
  -45m Lunch break
  13:00 - 17:30 Implementing the importer #project=478
    #ticket=ABC-123
  30m Code review #project="22/48.3"

2020-01-07 (5h15m!)
Three spaces of indentation
   3h #project=478 #ticket=ABC-123
   1h15m #meeting Weekly sync
   1h Writing C# code: a # without a name is not a tag

2020-01-08
A day off, so there are no entries #holiday

2020-01-09 (8h!)
Tags can have empty values, like #reviewed= or #reviewed=""
    <23:30 - 0:30 Overnight deployment #deploy
    9:00-12:00 No spaces around the dash
    12:00 - 12:00 Ranges can be empty
    1:00pm - 2:30pm #call='Bob "the builder"'
    119m Minutes can exceed 59 without an hour part
